GasAdsorptionLab

Python toolkit for automated DFT gas adsorption studies on 2D materials using ASE and Quantum ESPRESSO.

Features
---------
✔ Materials Project integration
✔ Surface generation
✔ Supercell creation
✔ Vacuum generation
✔ Adsorption site detection
✔ XYZ/CIF export
✔ QE input generation (coming)
✔ Symmetry reduction (coming)
✔ Automatic gas placement (coming)

Visualization examples
----------------------

```python
from ase.build import bulk
import numpy as np

from gal.gas import Gas
from gal.sites import Site
from gal.surface import Surface
from gal.adsorption import place_adsorbate
from gal.visualize import plot_top_sites, plot_bridge_sites, plot_hollow_sites

atoms = bulk("Si", cubic=True)
surface = Surface(atoms)
site = Site(name="Top", position=np.array([0.0, 0.0, 0.0]), neighbors=(0,), metadata={"kind": "top"})
gas = Gas("H2")

adsorbate = place_adsorbate(surface, gas, site, adsorption_height=2.0, rotation=45.0)
plot_top_sites(adsorbate, [site], show=False)

orientations = generate_orientations(gas.atoms, axes=("x", "z"), angles=(0.0, 90.0), n_per_axis=2)

qe_input = QEInput.from_config(config, atoms=adsorbate, prefix="adsorption")
qe_input.write("output/adsorption.in")

workflow = AdsorptionWorkflow(config=config, output_dir="output")
workflow.load_structure(atoms)
workflow.detect_sites()
workflow.generate_adsorption_configurations()
workflow.write_qe_inputs()
summary = workflow.run()
```

